<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>

<!--
Borg Backup - Unraid plugin for scheduled, deduplicated, encrypted backups of
Docker containers using BorgBackup. Every container is backed up unless it is
unticked, and you pick exactly which of each container's mounts get archived.

Follows the standard community plugin format, see:
https://wiki.unraid.net/Plugin_Development

Before cutting a release: run package.sh, which builds at the version below
(pass the "bump" flag to advance to a new one first), upload the printed .txz
to a GitHub release tagged with that version, then commit. package.sh writes
the MD5 into this file itself, so there is nothing to paste by hand.

Note for editors: a double hyphen is illegal inside an XML comment, and
xmllint reacts by dropping the whole DTD, which makes every entity below
"undefined". Spell out flag names here rather than writing them with dashes.

borg itself is not bundled. It is a ~26MB standalone binary with a
glibc-dependent build, so the plugin downloads the right one on first use via
Settings -> Utilities -> Borg Backup -> "Install / update borg", and keeps it
on the flash drive. /usr/local/bin is tmpfs, so the event/started hook
reinstates it on every boot.
-->

<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "borgbackup">
<!ENTITY author    "macmiller">
<!-- Version follows year.month.day.n - bump n for each same-day release,
     reset to 1 when the date changes. package.sh reads this value as its
     default (single source of truth) rather than generating its own. -->
<!ENTITY version   "2026.09.06.3">
<!-- Slackware identifies a package by stripping the last three hyphenated
     fields (version, arch, build), so the "x86_64-1" suffix is not decoration:
     without it upgradepkg cannot tell that a new .txz supersedes the installed
     one, installs it as a separate package, and leaves behind any file the old
     version had and the new one does not. -->
<!ENTITY txz       "&name;-&version;-x86_64-1.txz">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/macmillernz/unraid-borg-plugin/main/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY SRC       "https://github.com/macmillernz/unraid-borg-plugin/releases/download/&version;/&txz;">
<!-- MD5 of the .txz package.sh currently produces. package.sh rewrites this
     on every build; if it is stale the plugin manager refuses the download
     as corrupt. -->
<!ENTITY MD5       "49ce86cd1f69f0dc9a47e2842e24d967">
<!ENTITY emhttp    "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY configdir "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;"
        author="&author;"
        version="&version;"
        pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        launch="Utilities/Borg"
        icon="archive"
        min="6.12.0"
        support="https://github.com/macmillernz/unraid-borg-plugin/issues">

  <CHANGES>
###2026.09.06.3
- Fixed the install window sitting on "Starting..." forever when the installer
  produced no output. The status check only reported a failure if the log was
  non-empty, so a process that never started left the window spinning with
  nothing to show. It now reports that, and the button checks up front that the
  installer exists, is executable (repairing the mode if not) and actually
  spawned, naming the problem instead of hanging.
- The download no longer floods the window with curl's redraw meter. It reports
  megabytes as they arrive, so a ~26MB download visibly progresses.
- Falls back to plain nohup where setsid is unavailable.

###2026.09.06.2
- Fixed "Install / update borg" hanging forever. The ~26MB download ran inside
  the web request, which outlives the webserver's timeout, so the button spun
  and no result ever came back. It now runs detached.
- Added a live output window: the installer's progress and any errors appear as
  they happen, and the window stays open when it finishes so failures can be
  read.
- The build to download is now chosen from the release's real asset list and
  the server's own glibc version, instead of a hardcoded list of names. Upstream
  renamed these assets between 1.2, 1.4.1 and 1.4.5, and a build needing a newer
  glibc than the server has downloads fine and then refuses to run.

###2026.09.06.1
- The action buttons at the bottom of Settings now sit on one row, each sized
  to its own label. They were inside a definition list, which confined them to
  the narrow value column and wrapped them onto three rows at theme-imposed
  fixed widths.

###2026.09.05.3
- Fixed the plugin not appearing under Settings at all. The tabs were built
  from a Type="xmenu" parent page with Menu="Borg" sub-pages; that produced no
  menu entry. It is now a single page with the plain Menu="Utilities" header
  every simple plugin uses, and the Settings/Containers tabs are drawn by the
  plugin itself.
- Fixed packages being named without the arch and build fields. Slackware
  identifies a package by stripping the last three hyphenated fields, so
  upgradepkg could not tell one version from another and left removed files
  behind on upgrade. Packages are now name-version-x86_64-1.txz.
- Renamed one of the two sections both called "Archives".

###2026.09.05.2
- Fixed the second tab's title rendering as "Archives &amp;amp; Log". Page
  headers are not XML, so the entity was never decoded.
- Simplified to two tabs. The archive list, repository size and log moved to
  the bottom of Settings, under the buttons that produce them.
- Removed the "all containers / only selected" mode. It duplicated the tick
  boxes on the Containers tab. A container is now backed up unless you untick
  it, and one added later is included automatically.

###2026.09.05.1
- Initial release. Backs up Docker containers with BorgBackup on a schedule.
- Settings for repository location (local or ssh://), passphrase, archive
  naming format, compression, retention and schedule.
- All-containers or select-individually mode, and per-container selection of
  which bind mounts to archive, with optional stop/start around each archive
  and per-container exclude patterns.
- Retention is applied per container, so pruning one never touches another's
  archives.
  </CHANGES>

  <!-- Refuse to install where the PHP is too old for the plugin's code. -->
  <FILE Run="/bin/bash">
    <INLINE>
if [ ! -f /etc/unraid-version ]; then
  echo "This plugin only installs on Unraid."
  exit 1
fi
source /etc/unraid-version
if [ "$(printf '%s\n6.12.0\n' "$version" | sort -V | head -n1)" != "6.12.0" ]; then
  echo "Unraid 6.12.0 or newer is required (found $version)."
  exit 1
fi
    </INLINE>
  </FILE>

  <FILE Name="&configdir;/&txz;" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
    <URL>&SRC;</URL>
    <MD5>&MD5;</MD5>
  </FILE>

  <FILE Run="/bin/bash">
    <INLINE>
# Keep only the version we just installed.
find &configdir; -name "&name;-*.txz" ! -name "&txz;" -delete 2>/dev/null

mkdir -p &configdir;
[ -f &configdir;/passphrase ] &amp;&amp; chmod 600 &configdir;/passphrase 2>/dev/null

# /usr/local/bin is tmpfs; restore borg if a previous install already fetched it.
if [ -f &configdir;/borg ] &amp;&amp; [ ! -x /usr/local/bin/borg ]; then
  install -D -m 0755 &configdir;/borg /usr/local/bin/borg
fi

# Reinstate the schedule (a reinstall clears /etc/cron.d).
&emhttp;/scripts/borg-cron.sh >/dev/null 2>&amp;1

echo ""
echo "-----------------------------------------------------------"
echo " &name; &version; installed."
echo ""
if [ ! -x /usr/local/bin/borg ]; then
echo " Next: open Settings -> Utilities -> Borg Backup and press"
echo " 'Install / update borg' to download the borg binary, then"
echo " set your repository and passphrase."
else
echo " borg: $(/usr/local/bin/borg --version 2>/dev/null)"
fi
echo "-----------------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
    </INLINE>
  </FILE>

  <FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
    <INLINE>
rm -f /etc/cron.d/&name;
/usr/local/sbin/update_cron 2>/dev/null
removepkg &name; 2>/dev/null
rm -rf &emhttp;
rm -f &configdir;/&name;-*.txz

echo ""
echo " &name; removed."
echo " Settings, the borg binary and your passphrase were left in"
echo " &configdir; - delete that directory yourself if you want them gone."
echo " Your backup repository was not touched."
echo ""
    </INLINE>
  </FILE>

</PLUGIN>
